devin-search-mcp
================

This is a standalone [Model Context Protocol](https://modelcontextprotocol.io)
(MCP) server. It is a port of the `pi-devin-search` extension from
https://github.com/leafmoes/pi-devin-search (MIT License), which itself is a
port of https://github.com/mimimaster/dsh-devin-search (MIT License).

Portions of the OAuth (PKCE), web search, and read-only local code-search
protocol logic are adapted from those projects, which in turn credit
"piwin" (https://github.com/mimimaster/piwin, MIT) for the original
Windsurf/Codeium Connect/protobuf protocol implementation.

Upstream copyright and MIT license terms are preserved (see LICENSE). The
`lib/` directory is the upstream search core, kept as close to the reference
as practical so the ported surface is easy to diff. Only the host glue
(`main.js` in the PI-Desktop plugin) was rewritten here as `server.js` to run
as a stdio MCP server:

  - PI-Desktop `pi.fs.*`      -> a `node:fs` adapter (workspace-relative)
  - PI-Desktop `pi.net.fetch` -> global `fetch`
  - PI-Desktop workspace      -> process working directory / DEVIN_SEARCH_WORKSPACE
  - PI-Desktop panel login    -> a CLI command (`node server.js login`)
  - PI-Desktop tool registry  -> MCP `tools/list` + `tools/call`

One intentional deviation from upstream, in `lib/code-search.js`: an `rg`
command with a missing/empty pattern is rejected at command-validation time and
steered back to the planning model, instead of hard-failing the whole search
mid-execution. Upstream checked this only inside the sandbox, where it was
fatal, but the cloud planning model does emit malformed `rg` commands; this
makes code_search robust to them.
